#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055713} :activity/id #uuid "e7a68f82-01c3-5f8e-ac40-f72fcee7a2b7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049919 :topic/id #uuid "1e7769c8-1985-591a-bba8-e917166ea21d" :topic/math-academy-id 84} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055652 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054685 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054578 :question/id #uuid "5bb6861a-ea00-5644-bc16-d458cd2bb30f" :question/math-academy-id "e-7375"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae1738d1-3261-5769-ab80-0edcc76ab6f3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048652}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055380} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055509} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233089} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233769} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234449} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529091} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562500}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Y-Intercept of a Parabola Given Its Graph"} :step/id #uuid "128181ff-b771-504f-87d8-8018de0e4105" :step/math-academy-id 27352 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055716}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055713 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055952 :tutorial/content "Consider the graph of the parabola ![](images/f2/f218c572691a74963cd3808bf4df2923122e84b65d1fabf1138bab6264b043b5.svg) shown below.\n\n![](images/45/450251899f728a3cc927b72fdb7655204828c8e0be0432cb08cee2462d6e5bfe.png)\n\nWe can describe many features of the graph using mathematical terminology:\n\n- The ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-intercepts of the parabola are at ![](images/81/8171bb8403bd612f56ef5f32f400f1aef8efeed51ea279d36779771fdea1ae0d.svg) and ![](images/77/779cec712506e0f798805963ab85841b46650fb22681d97a64aec4b85a47d07f.svg) We say that ![](images/b0/b064281df4bef2506521322c7477468b9cc565616e2c5b6f21000df6522399c1.svg) and ![](images/1f/1fb9f2f73a09599931892c1dee7629975b4d851e5dd6f0d07b7c641bbf17bf54.svg) are the **roots** (or **zeros**) of the parabola.\n\n- The parabola intersects the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis at  ![](images/6a/6a0e2cbf9f56c3c989ad96f020fe8bb0f7c785ff6de8073c476232b95476ac13.svg). We say that ![](images/78/78d4465d85b55cee3832a9b598a2564b6a3fa9a072de8a1fb4b40ca884079670.svg) is the **![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-intercept**. The ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-intercept is the same as the constant term of the function.\n\n- The parabola has a \"turning point\" at  ![](images/ef/ef43561f9d825c9e79fb03dffafa744d386d0c2a5a07da903675bca120d59fd1.svg) which is called the **vertex**. In an upwards parabola (like the one shown above), the vertex is the minimum point, while in a downwards parabola, the vertex is the maximum point.\n\n- The vertical line  ![](images/df/df9822243c11ec9f0fabca5cc578976d0bdea2c521b4f61964f5f3850a970504.svg) that passes through the vertex is called the **axis of symmetry**. The part of the parabola to the left of the axis of symmetry is the mirror image of the right, and vice versa.\n\n- This particular parabola is **upward opening** because it has a distinctive ![](images/13/13ab0b72e7963f3e74404b8b75f12654ece94c2c44e1fb09fdf230b976eb681b.svg) shape. A parabola ![](images/7c/7c49eede8f0eb80dadd8384ae942dc8248ef454eeb6afa1aeba7ae48e7545456.svg) is upward opening if the quadratic coefficient is positive ![](images/d2/d2a0fc4d90b45e06999c89b1a40ff6f01116e9c429c195adbfced573f9e47660.svg)\n\n- Parabolas can also be **downward opening** with a distinctive ![](images/57/57872695daf3067460adec5a506cfb1457729de4eeac879eab9f7355570bac11.svg) shape. A parabola ![](images/7c/7c49eede8f0eb80dadd8384ae942dc8248ef454eeb6afa1aeba7ae48e7545456.svg) is downward opening if the quadratic coefficient is negative ![](images/a1/a16d199f292dbd74941402b3d485cf107a7a985d28aeb13ab50ff6baf87f2d4b.svg)\n\nLet's take a look at an example of a downward opening parabola." :tutorial/id #uuid "38157cb0-baf6-5463-917a-3e22397a6104" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1643 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "d642e4f2-9830-5f74-a1bf-20c4e26c8ac1" :step/math-academy-id 4546 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055714}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055714 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054720 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054486 :question/id #uuid "d7d8ce77-98d8-54d6-9684-edde0ba9e1ea" :question/math-academy-id "e-1450"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ec5627a-4a37-5a14-9b39-1b43b422171f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050763}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055158} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055159} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529127}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vertex and Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola Given Its Graph"} :step/id #uuid "f933d693-32d6-57d7-a9d6-8e75f0fb5999" :step/math-academy-id 4547 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055715}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055715 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054721 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054487 :question/id #uuid "7b9c1bbd-6d33-5fb8-a207-02cf71ba8b0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-1451"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa081d4-f85a-5239-b034-b78894429611" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049472}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055208} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055209} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233669} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233670} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529097} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529151} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529164} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529178} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562390} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562425}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Parabola Given Its Graph"} :step/id #uuid "4eea49a1-27f3-5ec1-8c5c-c52dee47ff51" :step/math-academy-id 4550 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055652}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055716 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054722 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054488 :question/id #uuid "d43441ff-4ab3-5cfd-ad5d-fbb6f82fa504" :question/math-academy-id "e-1452"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "867af724-0aa0-599a-8a5f-ee753fd19414" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050790}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055166} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055168} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529123} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529126} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562446} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562493}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Parabola Given Its Equation"} :step/id #uuid "ef88d516-7d9b-56b6-8c46-e0b80b4f034e" :step/math-academy-id 4553}] :activity/title "Graphs of General Quadratic Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054926}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562535} :activity/id #uuid "62106853-4525-5739-82c5-41ae5f174363" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049919 :topic/id #uuid "1e7769c8-1985-591a-bba8-e917166ea21d" :topic/math-academy-id 84} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562535 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42e07ce2-bc8b-58a5-9504-4e7eb9582a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6a/6ab5e5cdef936707ab8e9bd7fdc54c790ff4ce93cd3ef8af44aae44e8cd77764.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561744} {:answer/id #uuid "63e31f21-22da-5f21-b0c2-d0c9a0ddaefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f6/f671cee2e37f7905c220357782d2d4f2e6361d4858030084492e216d3f3031cd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561824} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e97a60-753f-5d6a-af1d-3fcdedc3559c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/07/0779906575c293797e031d96b507cdcbd5f6380dcd497ea2885c059da07d6da7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561996} {:answer/id #uuid "a94ecbb5-eea4-59d0-b204-e4dcc12c3179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8f/8fcd77fa59730639e108526ab31c73086db42e744353ff57a64f4df96c39a116.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562004} {:answer/id #uuid "b71126cb-562d-5bc2-bef7-a0e8477bbcdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b8/b868ef7ef919776ed69ceea87aefaa46787794353e5b390c27368fe5dd66b972.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561824} :answer-field/id #uuid "636c8023-db68-55b4-ae54-78725778fd9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c5c3534c-ace7-5657-a9dc-80aa55f51084" :question/math-academy-id "q-23981" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the graph of $y={x}^{2}-3x+5?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y={x}^{2}-3x+5.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=-1,0,1,2,3,4$ and then use the formula $y={x}^{2}-3x+5$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $9$ | $5$ | $3$ | $3$ | $5$ | $9$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/5a/5a7374c0e81f36d4d320abf38dcf72ac0b377c335894c601bfae82b64ea0bca3.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/f6/f671cee2e37f7905c220357782d2d4f2e6361d4858030084492e216d3f3031cd.png)"} :step/id #uuid "4cb68559-b2a9-5c4e-b09f-43ad55b721fe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562548}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562543 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43df9d15-0eff-56bd-ae68-6ce404601e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561747} {:answer/id #uuid "9d110e39-d8dd-5043-9919-f6ab4ffa4686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561969} {:answer/id #uuid "ac8df273-fbbd-50d2-a745-504e98301f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562012} {:answer/id #uuid "b0efac7a-0fd5-5b62-92bc-2e8956c2a791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562021} {:answer/id #uuid "fc271961-d308-50c2-8c91-fd71f82862ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562204}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561969} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce7f934-30bb-5661-a72f-65673ac7cfc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dcd95f6f-d031-5291-b596-6c28f4bcefd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-83559" :question/problem "![](images/ec/ecd951a63d500d0bf6b5234a65b8df55ada27882be337df6aea7d7aaa516e91b.png)\n\nThe equation of the curve above is $y=-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}x+k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}x+k \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{4}(0)^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we can find that $k=\\frac{1}{2}$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at \n$(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$"} :step/id #uuid "58f8528b-3855-50bb-b7e5-2d8a123cbd37" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562575}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562548 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cdb967f-21c2-5170-b53d-16d5028e4ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561620} {:answer/id #uuid "104e04eb-0268-563b-88fc-22075c061db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No roots" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561631} {:answer/id #uuid "756eb032-8a5b-5360-9dc8-c4731f589bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x=-1$ and $x=8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561872} {:answer/id #uuid "96957528-289f-58b7-a316-2d142247431e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561955} {:answer/id #uuid "a197812f-198c-576c-b3c5-5d39d4ceb48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x=1$ and $x=-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561983}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561631} :answer-field/id #uuid "88ac794d-2b1b-52d1-873f-37b7753f77b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3d69fa39-1eb4-5e90-8609-317c0513eaff" :question/math-academy-id "q-24637" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4e5c26cd78c9f3e778f5396b2cfda357042ddacc467783cb657ed9d5364665c4.png)\n\nFind the roots of the parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve does not intercept the $x$-axis.\n\nTherefore, the parabola does not have any roots."} :step/id #uuid "66993876-9b60-533e-8ab6-877b05f33c90" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562543}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562575 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38fc099c-e039-58f8-895c-1d8133c2ca8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x=-6$ and $x=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561725} {:answer/id #uuid "495e48c1-6950-556c-8281-4a67734449a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x=-5$ and $x=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561769} {:answer/id #uuid "70b07e97-42ce-5dd2-877a-991c6029d372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x=5$ and $x=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561861} {:answer/id #uuid "7d12d4cd-fcdc-53fc-bfc0-f0337c4ca438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561892} {:answer/id #uuid "ba5c8a8b-cbde-534e-9ea3-176b5d4ad019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$x=-2$ and $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562058}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561769} :answer-field/id #uuid "31585cc3-c8a8-5d1a-b60d-72ee74673b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "01c1b80a-b0c5-5bb0-af0e-20dd6de4f28c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106033" :question/problem "![](images/a0/a0953e1812fb96b65ec77816caf08049052173ab04e76b9f101a3eee52d5ae8b.png)\n\nFind the roots of the parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-5,0)$ and $(2,0).$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-5$ and $x=2.$"} :step/id #uuid "cc087953-4c06-57cb-9fb5-54f19a275ac7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562586}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562586 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7677ae-e62e-5829-91f7-2020875a297a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ba/ba70051173652d8783cc8ebd9f200b5dcdf37cda8d81a772c0160e01c31cbf32.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561615} {:answer/id #uuid "21653903-a8ae-5843-86a3-6e201dd68978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/00/007a6abdf7787cc14e40c3d92996d5224904a656f8fa6ef42a9911ce97bc24a6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561674} {:answer/id #uuid "496c5471-4221-5e19-a1ab-408227761210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c3/c34cebb49b0482f02872a1ba68f73f8e931d8fb6583daf653560fc17f5b4831d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561770} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ac50e9-41c5-5f35-8129-bb0c31f3b0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ae/ae303cc7bd52ab5c6c5eb19f0ed3abe6286f560d58b6c21c78bac4758e978774.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561981} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3011dc-818d-5565-8b19-02f93ab49957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/cf/cfd42d5e800218639a82bbe46a0749bc3788c616fedc43cb704ebea9448a5867.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562165}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561674} :answer-field/id #uuid "758cf8be-30e9-58cb-b2f3-197f61860574" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7984db9b-dab8-5221-ba35-8d0a5e549cba" :question/math-academy-id "q-106059" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the graph of $y={x}^{2}-x-6?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y={x}^{2}-x-6.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=-2,-1,0,1,2,3$ and then use the formula $y={x}^{2}-x-6$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row. \n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $0$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $0$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/4f/4fbf87172434c03bbdff6967d03eae3146f016dcdbb9422e89d2d94ab7693cd5.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/00/007a6abdf7787cc14e40c3d92996d5224904a656f8fa6ef42a9911ce97bc24a6.png)"} :step/id #uuid "eabe0eed-285b-5b48-981b-8b06bc81b02c"}] :activity/title "Graphs of General Quadratic Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561570}]}
